WEBVTT

00:08.968 --> 00:12.137
Somebody sent Addison
to burn down my house.

00:12.138 --> 00:13.555
I want you to find out who it is.

00:13.556 --> 00:15.306
It's Cat Hardy. He finds out

00:15.307 --> 00:17.851
she was behind it, he'll kill her.

00:17.852 --> 00:19.853
Only money tells the truth.

00:19.854 --> 00:22.397
Crafty bastard
marks all of his bills.

00:22.398 --> 00:25.483
I don't care if Silvermane hired you.
I'm gonna find the rat.

00:25.484 --> 00:27.153
Come on, Gio.

00:29.196 --> 00:31.322
I met this guy
at the Hooverville.

00:31.323 --> 00:33.324
He knows both Addison
and Flint Marko.

00:33.325 --> 00:34.451
What are the chances?

00:37.371 --> 00:40.415
Crime is out of control.
The city needs order.

00:40.416 --> 00:42.125
Get me in touch with The Spider.

00:42.126 --> 00:43.543
If you love me,

00:43.544 --> 00:44.628
you'll leave with me right now.

00:45.379 --> 00:46.546
There's no turning it off!

00:46.547 --> 00:48.006
I am done with people telling me

00:48.007 --> 00:49.799
who I am and what I get to do.

00:49.800 --> 00:51.761
There you are.

00:53.262 --> 00:54.679
Did you know that I mark all my bills?

00:54.680 --> 00:56.765
Guess where I mark yours.

00:56.766 --> 00:58.224
You son of a bitch.

00:58.225 --> 00:59.434
You set me up.

00:59.435 --> 01:02.520
I'll rip your goddamn--

01:02.521 --> 01:03.731
We'll be needing another grave.

01:11.238 --> 01:16.659
♪ No place to hide when ♪

01:16.660 --> 01:23.667
♪ his devilish eyes start smiling ♪

01:24.335 --> 01:28.422
♪ start smiling ♪

01:29.507 --> 01:32.967
♪ These kind of nights ♪

01:32.968 --> 01:35.053
♪ lend ♪

01:35.054 --> 01:39.390
♪ a subtle nod to ♪

01:39.391 --> 01:41.727
♪ crying ♪

01:43.479 --> 01:46.648
♪ a loud silence...

01:46.649 --> 01:48.650
Yeah, Winston was a stone-cold killer.

01:48.651 --> 01:52.737
A useful weapon in my arsenal,
but entirely replaceable.

01:52.738 --> 01:54.614
Same goes for his pal Gio.

01:59.078 --> 02:04.165
♪ What's worse? The cold? ♪

02:04.166 --> 02:08.503
♪ Or the devil that you know...

02:08.504 --> 02:09.587
It was risky,

02:09.588 --> 02:11.381
not letting me in on your plans,

02:11.382 --> 02:14.426
but it was a smart play, start to finish.

02:15.427 --> 02:17.220
Are you listening to me?

02:17.221 --> 02:19.180
I'm trying to pay you a compliment.

02:22.935 --> 02:24.727
You did a good job.

02:24.728 --> 02:26.187
Smart.

02:26.188 --> 02:28.274
Patient.

02:29.567 --> 02:31.818
I could use someone like you
on my payroll.

02:31.819 --> 02:35.154
I'm not a fan of your retirement plan.

02:35.155 --> 02:37.741
You got some mouth.

02:40.744 --> 02:43.122
Could get you killed some day.

02:46.834 --> 02:48.460
♪ Oh ♪

02:49.086 --> 02:52.630
♪ No place to hide when...

02:52.631 --> 02:55.174
Talking to the police chief tomorrow.

02:55.175 --> 02:57.136
He on the payroll, too?

02:58.387 --> 03:00.847
Why is he running raids
on your booze shipments?

03:00.848 --> 03:02.807
Exactly.

03:02.808 --> 03:06.854
♪ with the devil you ♪

03:08.397 --> 03:14.694
♪ know ♪

03:19.783 --> 03:21.368
She's not bad, huh?

03:22.369 --> 03:23.913
Beautiful, Cat.

03:25.164 --> 03:27.333
It'd be a shame to have to kill her.

03:29.877 --> 03:31.377
Beautiful song.

03:31.378 --> 03:33.546
- You wrote it?
- I did.

03:33.547 --> 03:35.423
We prefer the splashier numbers.

03:35.424 --> 03:36.841
I thought we were celebrating.

03:36.842 --> 03:40.011
- Killing people?
- A couple of rats...

03:40.012 --> 03:41.930
who tried to put you in a hole.

03:41.931 --> 03:43.432
Reilly kept you out of it.

03:44.475 --> 03:46.768
I'll drink to that.

03:46.769 --> 03:49.896
Any regrets on the fact
you almost killed me for nothing tonight?

03:49.897 --> 03:51.898
Yeah, I don't dwell.

03:51.899 --> 03:53.191
Maybe you should start.

03:53.192 --> 03:56.194
Well, it's getting late.

03:56.195 --> 03:57.904
Ah, no. No chance.

03:57.905 --> 03:59.948
You and me are drinking tonight.

03:59.949 --> 04:02.450
Be a doll and grab us a bottle
of the Yellow Spot.

04:02.451 --> 04:04.243
Enjoy the Spot whiskey.

04:04.244 --> 04:05.913
We're going up a notch.

04:38.112 --> 04:40.780
♪ The colors fading from the photograph ♪

04:40.781 --> 04:42.532
♪ I could tell the story ♪

04:42.533 --> 04:45.201
♪ but still you wouldn't know the half ♪

04:45.202 --> 04:47.996
♪ This love was brought to life
from shards of glass ♪

04:47.997 --> 04:50.081
♪ When you kiss me there's a shifting ♪

04:50.082 --> 04:52.542
♪ in the sepia tone ♪

04:52.543 --> 04:55.753
♪ Can't escape the madness,
baby, magnetism ♪

04:55.754 --> 04:59.090
♪ Run away but something
pulls me back into it ♪

04:59.091 --> 05:02.218
♪ Lately I've been staring
at a broken mirror ♪

05:02.219 --> 05:05.680
♪ Needing someone to call my own ♪

05:05.681 --> 05:08.891
♪ Hey, lover ♪

05:08.892 --> 05:11.769
♪ I need someone to save me now ♪

05:11.770 --> 05:14.022
♪ from all the pain ♪

05:14.023 --> 05:16.482
♪ I suffer ♪

05:16.483 --> 05:19.318
♪ and the heavy world
that weighs me down ♪

05:19.319 --> 05:22.864
♪ 'Cause the world ain't sweet ♪

05:22.865 --> 05:25.241
♪ It's bitter to taste ♪

05:25.242 --> 05:26.617
♪ But you could be ♪

05:26.618 --> 05:29.830
♪ my saving grace ♪

05:56.065 --> 05:57.523
Please assure him

05:57.524 --> 06:00.069
that I will have Mr. Reilly
return his call as soon as he's in.

06:00.861 --> 06:04.031
Yes, I'll be sure to add that
to your previous messages.

06:05.032 --> 06:06.366
Mm-hmm.

06:09.078 --> 06:10.828
- Mayor again?
- Uh-huh.

06:10.829 --> 06:12.623
Does he know
which Ben Reilly he's calling?

06:16.585 --> 06:18.795
Goddamn it!

06:21.799 --> 06:23.216
This goddamn guy.

06:24.718 --> 06:26.303
Jesus Christ.

06:30.557 --> 06:32.100
Wow. I--

06:32.101 --> 06:33.560
Okay.

06:40.943 --> 06:42.777
Say what you will about Silvermane,

06:42.778 --> 06:45.446
but I admire the man's constitution.

06:45.447 --> 06:46.906
He can drink.

06:46.907 --> 06:48.407
- Any idea why the mayor's so keen...
- I got a tip

06:48.408 --> 06:49.617
- that Lonnie's in Harlem.
- ...to talk to you?

06:49.618 --> 06:50.701
So I'm gonna head uptown, see if I can

06:50.702 --> 06:51.953
- make amends for that bullshit Bugle...
- Because he's called the office

06:51.954 --> 06:53.037
- nine times and counting. Nine.
- ...story Walters ran yesterday.

06:53.038 --> 06:54.872
- Scrambled.
- Excuse me?

06:54.873 --> 06:57.834
I need scrambled eggs and...

06:57.835 --> 06:59.252
sausages.

06:59.253 --> 07:00.753
And...

07:00.754 --> 07:02.130
a biscuit.

07:02.131 --> 07:05.092
If we're dreaming, why don't you add gravy
to that, Mr. Moneybags?

07:09.346 --> 07:11.139
Holy shit.

07:11.140 --> 07:12.765
I'm not even gonna ask.

07:12.766 --> 07:14.433
That's probably wise.

07:14.434 --> 07:16.269
Please. I need food.

07:16.270 --> 07:17.563
After you talk to the mayor.

07:18.856 --> 07:21.399
- God.
- I'm gonna head out and look for Lonnie.

07:21.400 --> 07:23.067
Let me know how it goes in...

07:23.068 --> 07:25.487
♪ Harlem ♪

07:30.325 --> 07:32.618
Who am I?

07:32.619 --> 07:34.829
Well, that would be you.

08:29.343 --> 08:31.010
Sleep well, sunshine?

08:31.011 --> 08:33.012
Like a kitten.

08:33.013 --> 08:34.597
Why do you ask?

08:34.598 --> 08:36.850
A guy can't inquire
after his favorite gal?

08:43.315 --> 08:45.650
Truth is, I was up all night.

08:45.651 --> 08:47.276
Too much adrenaline from yesterday.

08:49.988 --> 08:51.739
Maybe I wasn't the only one.

08:51.740 --> 08:53.366
What did you put through the wall?

08:53.367 --> 08:56.494
My fist, my head, bust of Caesar.

08:56.495 --> 08:58.121
What does it matter?

09:04.670 --> 09:06.712
Wouldn't want you catching a cold.

09:06.713 --> 09:08.256
Lose your voice,

09:08.257 --> 09:09.924
miss a show.

09:09.925 --> 09:11.885
I haven't missed a show in seven years.

09:13.220 --> 09:15.597
You almost missed one last night,
though, didn't you?

09:16.473 --> 09:18.599
If you have something to say, say it.

09:18.600 --> 09:20.351
It's too early for subtext.

09:20.352 --> 09:21.645
Text, then.

09:24.773 --> 09:27.358
Winston was the rat...

09:27.359 --> 09:30.237
but that doesn't answer
what you were doing at the train station.

09:39.329 --> 09:40.663
Why don't you ask Winston?

09:40.664 --> 09:43.165
- Can't.
- And why is that?

09:43.166 --> 09:44.959
'Cause I put a bullet in his chest.

09:44.960 --> 09:47.378
And if the P.I. had told you
I was the rat?

09:47.379 --> 09:49.298
I'd have put a bullet in you.

09:50.340 --> 09:52.301
Well, there's your answer.

09:55.387 --> 09:56.805
That's not an answer.

09:58.056 --> 09:59.516
And it's not the truth.

10:01.810 --> 10:04.061
The truth is I was terrified.

10:04.062 --> 10:06.814
Not because I was guilty,
but because you were unhinged.

10:06.815 --> 10:10.652
Looking to lash out
and feel like you're still invulnerable.

10:11.695 --> 10:13.572
There you go. Now we are talking.

10:14.740 --> 10:16.949
Why was Reilly with you at the station?

10:16.950 --> 10:19.368
He wasn't with me.

10:19.369 --> 10:21.287
He was watching me.

10:21.288 --> 10:22.538
For you.

10:22.539 --> 10:23.914
He must have figured out

10:23.915 --> 10:27.502
Winston was the rat and thought
I was in on it because I was running.

10:28.628 --> 10:32.007
He didn't know I had nothing to do
with it until Winston tried to frame me.

10:37.387 --> 10:38.805
Good.

10:41.683 --> 10:44.435
Reilly was smart not to trust anyone.

10:44.436 --> 10:46.645
And he was smart not to play favorites.

10:46.646 --> 10:49.106
If he's so smart,
then why don't you hire him?

10:49.107 --> 10:51.150
I tried.

10:51.151 --> 10:52.735
He was smart enough to say no.

10:55.197 --> 10:56.280
I'm glad you're back.

10:56.281 --> 10:58.324
No place I'd rather be.

10:59.743 --> 11:01.370
That's my girl.

11:07.876 --> 11:10.253
See? There you go.
I knew you could do it.

11:17.969 --> 11:21.222
- The desk wobbles.
- I'm aware. Focus.

11:21.223 --> 11:22.848
How am I supposed to focus
on a wobbly desk?

11:22.849 --> 11:25.351
Trust me, I've been asking
that same question for three days now.

11:27.062 --> 11:29.439
Listen, I don't know
how many times I have to tell you--

11:30.774 --> 11:32.274
I am so sorry.

11:32.275 --> 11:34.694
Uh, yes. Reilly Investigations.
May I ask who's calling?

11:36.196 --> 11:38.280
Hi... Ms. Hardy.

11:38.281 --> 11:41.159
Mr. Reilly isn't here at the moment.
Would you like me to take a message?

11:42.619 --> 11:43.578
Uh-huh.

11:44.955 --> 11:45.831
Yeah.

11:46.832 --> 11:49.417
Three p.m. The Calypso.

11:49.418 --> 11:50.836
Yeah, I'll let him know.

11:52.129 --> 11:53.796
- School's out.
- Ah, yes.

11:53.797 --> 11:55.006
Find Ben. Give him this.

11:58.510 --> 12:00.512
And we're not done here.

12:03.390 --> 12:05.182
Oh, Johnny Cave.

12:05.183 --> 12:07.143
Well, of course. A great guy.

12:07.144 --> 12:08.477
He told me so himself.

12:08.478 --> 12:09.812
You wouldn't doubt it,
would you?

12:09.813 --> 12:11.272
Same place, 12:30.

12:11.273 --> 12:12.440
- And don't be late.
- And don't be late.

12:12.441 --> 12:14.775
What? Me late? Well, I like that.

12:14.776 --> 12:16.986
Of all the nerve.
What are you talking about?

12:16.987 --> 12:18.320
I'm usually the one
that has to stand around

12:18.321 --> 12:19.530
waiting 20 minutes for you to show up.

12:19.531 --> 12:20.781
-  All right, all right.
- All right, all right.

12:20.782 --> 12:22.533
- All right, all right, all right.
- All right, all right, all right.

12:22.534 --> 12:23.909
But you heard me.

12:23.910 --> 12:25.453
- Don't be late.
- Don't be late.

12:34.546 --> 12:35.714
- Red hot.
- Red hot.

13:01.698 --> 13:03.157
No.

13:03.158 --> 13:05.201
Ben, it's me. Open up!

13:06.578 --> 13:08.162
I'm sleeping.

13:08.163 --> 13:09.414
Then how you talking?

13:10.415 --> 13:11.540
Did you hear me?

13:11.541 --> 13:12.875
If you sleeping, how are you talking?

13:12.876 --> 13:14.376
What?

13:14.377 --> 13:17.129
Singer left a message with Janet.
She said it was important.

13:17.130 --> 13:18.465
Quit school early and everything.

13:19.216 --> 13:21.676
Ah, now he's awake.

13:22.761 --> 13:24.970
Anyways, I'd better run.

13:24.971 --> 13:26.972
- Yeah.
- But--

13:26.973 --> 13:28.766
Maybe a shower.

13:30.393 --> 13:31.936
And a shave.

13:31.937 --> 13:34.231
And a fresh shirt.

13:35.440 --> 13:36.942
And-and good-good luck.

13:50.789 --> 13:52.666
More coffee, boss?

13:56.753 --> 13:58.504
More coffee?

13:58.505 --> 14:00.298
You think I'm deaf.

14:01.299 --> 14:03.968
- Is that it?
- No. I...

14:03.969 --> 14:05.512
I just...

14:15.063 --> 14:18.023
I don't think
Chief McNamara's coming, boss.

14:21.861 --> 14:24.572
Then find him, and remind him

14:24.573 --> 14:28.450
that one of the conditions
of his palms getting greased

14:28.451 --> 14:32.831
is showing up
for his weekly appointment.

14:37.168 --> 14:38.962
And clean that up.

14:49.306 --> 14:50.764
- You made it.
- I did.

14:50.765 --> 14:52.349
Think I owe you a drink.

14:52.350 --> 14:55.102
A little later.
Our mutual friend bought me plenty.

14:55.103 --> 14:58.063
We need to talk about that.
Get our stories straight.

14:58.064 --> 15:00.774
He wanted to know why you were with me
at the train station last night.

15:00.775 --> 15:02.943
- And you said?
- That you didn't trust me.

15:02.944 --> 15:04.653
Thought I might be
in cahoots with Winston.

15:04.654 --> 15:06.655
- Smart.
- He's smart, too.

15:06.656 --> 15:08.699
And he won't stop with Winston.

15:08.700 --> 15:11.493
He'll start asking questions
about the raid, which might lead him to--

15:11.494 --> 15:13.287
Mayor?

15:13.288 --> 15:15.497
I think I underestimated you.

15:15.498 --> 15:16.915
Happens.

15:16.916 --> 15:18.709
Seriously, why are you doing this?

15:18.710 --> 15:20.169
Why did you try to kill Silvermane?

15:20.170 --> 15:22.213
- I asked you first.
- I saved your life.

15:25.425 --> 15:26.884
Not here.

15:30.472 --> 15:32.556
One and two and hop and fly.

15:35.101 --> 15:36.560
Don't worry, friends.

15:36.561 --> 15:38.437
There's plenty of soup to go around.

15:46.780 --> 15:49.073
- Two?
- Oh, you got it, boss.

15:49.074 --> 15:50.783
How's business?

15:50.784 --> 15:52.160
Well, you just doubled it.

15:55.288 --> 15:56.330
So...

15:56.331 --> 15:58.457
You serve your country,
and this is how they repay you.

15:58.458 --> 16:00.209
Everyone's gonna eat today.

16:00.210 --> 16:02.753
- Are you a vet, too?
- Oh, no, no, no, no.

16:02.754 --> 16:05.089
I'm a journalist.

16:05.090 --> 16:07.341
In fact, I'm looking for someone
named Lonnie Lincoln.

16:07.342 --> 16:09.426
- Ah.
- Doing a story on Black vets

16:09.427 --> 16:11.470
and how their lives turned out.

16:11.471 --> 16:13.222
Well, you in the right place.

16:13.223 --> 16:16.266
All the vets in Harlem are about
to line up to get their hot meals.

16:16.267 --> 16:17.643
- Oh, yeah?
- Yeah.

16:17.644 --> 16:19.561
But you want stories?

16:19.562 --> 16:21.605
I got stories for days.

16:21.606 --> 16:24.817
Hey, picture this.
Case of anchovies falls off

16:24.818 --> 16:26.235
- the back of a truck.
- Yeah.

16:26.236 --> 16:27.653
- Now, my man Steven?
- Steven.

16:27.654 --> 16:29.905
He's gathering up
all the anchovies and cans.

16:29.906 --> 16:31.990
He don't even like anchovies.

16:31.991 --> 16:34.077
Now I'm like Steven.
I don't even like anchovies.

16:35.370 --> 16:36.954
What is this place?

16:36.955 --> 16:38.832
My old life.

16:40.500 --> 16:43.586
It's where I used to perform
before Silvermane found me.

16:44.754 --> 16:46.463
I used to sing for pennies.

16:46.464 --> 16:50.217
Could barely afford
to put food in my stomach, but...

16:50.218 --> 16:52.011
I loved it.

16:53.680 --> 16:57.850
One night, Silvermane tipped me more money
than I'd ever seen in my life.

16:57.851 --> 16:59.643
Next day, he made a proposal.

16:59.644 --> 17:01.687
Headline a new club.

17:01.688 --> 17:03.814
Said I'd have everything
I could ever want.

17:03.815 --> 17:05.649
And he gave it to me.

17:05.650 --> 17:07.568
But you couldn't see the strings.

17:07.569 --> 17:09.403
They were thin at first,

17:09.404 --> 17:11.448
but over the years,
they got thick as rope.

17:13.283 --> 17:15.033
No.

17:15.034 --> 17:17.035
They were never like that.

17:17.036 --> 17:20.456
The only thing
Silvermane gets off on is power.

17:20.457 --> 17:22.458
As long as he can control what I wear,

17:22.459 --> 17:24.293
what I do,

17:24.294 --> 17:26.671
who I'm around...

17:42.812 --> 17:44.897
There was a man once.

17:44.898 --> 17:46.524
Thomas.

17:47.525 --> 17:50.027
Started coming to the club
night after night.

17:50.028 --> 17:53.447
And, eventually...

17:53.448 --> 17:54.657
he wore me down.

17:55.742 --> 17:58.160
He was a dentist, if you can believe it.

17:58.161 --> 18:00.871
Sexy dentist, huh?

18:00.872 --> 18:03.040
Yeah, I heard about those guys.

18:03.041 --> 18:06.251
Oh, no, but he was kind.

18:06.252 --> 18:10.840
And I guess, for me,
kindness was something new.

18:13.885 --> 18:17.721
After about a year,
he surprised me with a ring.

18:17.722 --> 18:21.351
And I surprised him by saying "yes."

18:24.896 --> 18:27.397
After Thomas suddenly stopped coming by,

18:27.398 --> 18:30.985
I thought
maybe I had done something wrong.

18:39.285 --> 18:41.745
Could have just scared him off,

18:41.746 --> 18:43.581
but Silvermane had him killed.

18:44.666 --> 18:47.085
Wanted to make sure
I'd never make the same mistake again.

18:48.753 --> 18:52.047
But you did... with Flint.

18:52.048 --> 18:55.634
I suppose he's kind, too,
when he isn't busting heads.

18:55.635 --> 18:57.970
He is, in fact.

18:57.971 --> 19:02.599
He's got more honor and loyalty
than anyone I know,

19:02.600 --> 19:04.978
so I thought
I would give us both a second chance.

19:06.938 --> 19:10.232
And to do it,
you needed Silvermane out of the picture.

19:10.233 --> 19:13.987
I was so dumb to think
that maybe I could have it all.

19:17.991 --> 19:21.118
Tell me about Addison.

19:21.119 --> 19:23.579
Flint mentioned him.

19:23.580 --> 19:25.205
They were war buddies.

19:25.206 --> 19:27.124
He was worried about him.

19:27.125 --> 19:29.710
Said Jimmy lost his job.

19:29.711 --> 19:31.670
That he'd been burning things for money.

19:31.671 --> 19:34.089
Mostly insurance scams.

19:34.090 --> 19:36.258
With the money I was offering,

19:36.259 --> 19:38.511
it wasn't hard to convince him
to kill Silvermane.

19:39.596 --> 19:41.638
But Addison botched the job

19:41.639 --> 19:44.266
and let Silvermane get away.

19:44.267 --> 19:45.976
Oh.

19:45.977 --> 19:49.062
And then that other freak--

19:49.063 --> 19:52.441
what's he called? The Spider? --

19:52.442 --> 19:54.693
ruined your second try.

19:54.694 --> 19:57.155
- And here we are.
- Hmm.

20:02.493 --> 20:05.370
So, if-if there ain't chicken,
and there ain't noodles,

20:05.371 --> 20:08.123
then it ain't chicken noodle soup,
is it? It's...

20:08.124 --> 20:10.834
It's just soup. You know what I mean?

20:10.835 --> 20:15.130
Are you gonna get this down?
'Cause I'm-I'm spitting gold here.

20:15.131 --> 20:17.341
I got it all up here.

20:17.342 --> 20:21.595
Harvey, my friend,
thanks for the perspective.

20:21.596 --> 20:23.805
You got it.
Hey, hey, don't be a stranger.

20:23.806 --> 20:28.810
I'm here all day, every day,
rain or shine.

21:11.229 --> 21:13.438
- I'm alone, no cops.
- I should rip your head off.

21:13.439 --> 21:15.107
I know, but listen.

21:15.108 --> 21:17.610
The story they printed
wasn't what I gave 'em.

21:18.444 --> 21:20.988
- Now, I came here to make things right.
- You expect me to believe that?

21:20.989 --> 21:22.699
Brother, let me help you.

21:23.783 --> 21:26.827
At least let's go somewhere
more comfortable and talk.

21:26.828 --> 21:28.829
The Alcove. 79th and--

21:28.830 --> 21:30.497
Yeah, I know where The Alcove is.

21:30.498 --> 21:32.332
Everybody knows where The Alcove is.

21:32.333 --> 21:34.209
Evening, Ms. Hardy.

21:34.210 --> 21:37.629
- Good evening.
- How about those monster freaks, huh?

21:37.630 --> 21:39.214
What a mess.

21:39.215 --> 21:40.757
You think
The Spider's gonna show back up?

21:40.758 --> 21:43.093
I doubt it. I mean, the guy could barely
hack it when he was the only--

21:43.094 --> 21:45.388
Maybe just the ride, if you don't mind?

21:46.973 --> 21:48.891
Mm-hmm. Sure thing, pal.

21:57.316 --> 21:59.609
I don't think I can be alone tonight.

22:05.450 --> 22:08.285
Hey, do you mind going back downtown?

22:08.286 --> 22:10.538
Yeah. Sure thing, pal.

22:21.549 --> 22:23.091
Look who finally showed up.

22:23.092 --> 22:25.552
You found the police chief?

22:25.553 --> 22:27.555
Even better.

22:29.599 --> 22:31.309
My boy!

22:32.310 --> 22:33.810
Where have you been?

22:33.811 --> 22:35.979
Been looking all over the city for you.

22:35.980 --> 22:37.856
I had to lay low for a minute.

22:37.857 --> 22:39.566
Yeah, you did.

22:39.567 --> 22:43.070
You're in all the papers
after that number you did on those cops.

22:43.071 --> 22:45.072
Yeah.

22:45.073 --> 22:47.158
Where did all that come from, son?

22:48.409 --> 22:50.118
Don't worry about it.

22:50.119 --> 22:52.204
I'm just glad you're back.

22:52.205 --> 22:54.623
You hear we had a traitor in our midst?

22:56.834 --> 22:58.503
You never did like Winston, did you?

22:59.837 --> 23:01.088
Winston?

23:01.089 --> 23:03.381
You thought it was someone else?

23:03.382 --> 23:05.175
Me, too.

23:05.176 --> 23:07.844
That's why
you can never really trust anyone.

23:07.845 --> 23:10.555
Even the staunchest of allies.

23:10.556 --> 23:13.434
Money, power. They can corrupt anybody.

23:18.773 --> 23:20.483
You all right?

23:26.989 --> 23:28.366
It's okay.

23:29.659 --> 23:31.410
You're welcome here, no matter what.

23:32.495 --> 23:34.038
You've always been loyal.

23:35.248 --> 23:37.249
That cuts both ways, Flint.

23:37.250 --> 23:40.377
You watch my back, and I watch yours.

23:40.378 --> 23:42.462
Got to warn you, though.

23:42.463 --> 23:44.298
We've got a fight coming.

23:45.299 --> 23:47.677
- Are you ready for that?
- I'm ready.

23:49.095 --> 23:52.222
Whatever you need, I'm ready.

23:52.223 --> 23:54.182
Good.

23:54.183 --> 23:56.894
Time to show the mayor
what he's up against.

24:03.693 --> 24:05.277
Should we...

24:05.278 --> 24:06.988
talk about the powers?

24:09.949 --> 24:11.450
When you got 'em?

24:16.664 --> 24:18.123
Or just-- Where you from?

24:18.124 --> 24:20.376
You a Harlem kid?

25:00.499 --> 25:02.043
You a card player?

25:03.127 --> 25:05.045
Played a few hands here and there.

25:05.046 --> 25:07.256
Oh, so you're good, huh?

25:24.607 --> 25:26.441
Ah.

25:26.442 --> 25:28.735
It's not much.

25:28.736 --> 25:29.946
You don't have to do that.

25:31.239 --> 25:32.781
Do what?

25:32.782 --> 25:34.200
Be humble.

25:38.120 --> 25:41.081
Hmm. Do you have anything to drink?

25:41.082 --> 25:44.794
Sure. Um, well, uh,
how about some music? You know, and...?

25:47.922 --> 25:49.590
Ah...

25:51.884 --> 25:53.219
Uh...

25:54.637 --> 25:56.429
...there's only one glass.

25:56.430 --> 25:58.557
I haven't had many guests.

25:59.558 --> 26:00.559
Ben...

26:02.103 --> 26:05.772
Oh. Well, here's another, but it's used.

26:05.773 --> 26:07.566
I'll just use the used glass.

26:08.651 --> 26:11.444
♪ Sleep will banish sorrow ♪

26:13.364 --> 26:17.450
♪ Tears and parting ♪

26:17.451 --> 26:20.037
♪ They make us forlorn ♪

26:20.913 --> 26:23.499
♪ But with the dawn ♪

26:24.583 --> 26:26.543
Take a seat, make yourself comfortable.

26:26.544 --> 26:29.045
♪ A new day is born...

26:29.046 --> 26:30.839
So, here we are.

26:30.840 --> 26:32.717
Here we are.

26:33.759 --> 26:35.720
Your turn.

26:36.512 --> 26:38.723
Tell me why.

26:39.640 --> 26:41.225
Right, my turn.

26:42.101 --> 26:43.978
My turn.

26:45.229 --> 26:48.148
♪ Still my love will guide you...

26:48.149 --> 26:49.733
There was this girl.

26:49.734 --> 26:51.860
This, uh,

26:51.861 --> 26:54.071
smart, fun girl.

26:55.072 --> 26:57.033
You want to tell me about her?

26:59.285 --> 27:01.746
♪ Good night, sweetheart...

27:02.830 --> 27:06.000
Her name was Ruby, and, um, we were...

27:07.126 --> 27:08.543
...happy.

27:24.727 --> 27:26.895
And I did a job. No big deal.

27:26.896 --> 27:28.688
Deadbeat husband, but,

27:28.689 --> 27:31.441
he ended up doing five years hard time,

27:31.442 --> 27:35.945
and he got through the stint
thinking about one thing--

27:35.946 --> 27:37.448
revenge.

27:39.742 --> 27:43.620
I still don't know how,
but he knew I was close to Ruby,

27:43.621 --> 27:45.915
and he killed her.

27:48.125 --> 27:49.876
I...  I was

27:49.877 --> 27:53.005
going to take her to dinner
on that night.

27:56.967 --> 27:59.052
The fact is, we never made it to dinner,

27:59.053 --> 28:03.098
because I was too busy getting drunk...

28:04.183 --> 28:06.894
...in a bar across town
to know she was in danger.

28:08.020 --> 28:10.563
And I got there too late.

28:29.083 --> 28:31.543
He killed her to make me suffer.

28:31.544 --> 28:34.003
He killed her, but...

28:34.004 --> 28:36.006
I'm the reason she's dead.

28:41.303 --> 28:44.682
If Ruby had never met me,
she'd still be alive.

28:45.683 --> 28:47.517
♪ But with the dawn...

28:47.518 --> 28:48.894
So...

28:50.563 --> 28:53.356
...you saved me
to make up for not saving her.

28:53.357 --> 28:54.899
Nothing can make up for that.

28:54.900 --> 28:58.821
I did it so I wouldn't feel any worse.

29:01.073 --> 29:03.116
So how do you feel?

29:03.117 --> 29:04.617
How do I feel?

29:04.618 --> 29:06.578
Uh...

29:09.790 --> 29:11.667
Alone.

29:14.253 --> 29:15.503
♪ Dreams enfold you...

29:15.504 --> 29:17.006
Well...

29:18.174 --> 29:20.759
...maybe we can be alone together.

29:23.095 --> 29:27.641
♪ Good night, sweetheart ♪

29:28.767 --> 29:31.686
♪ Good night ♪

29:33.272 --> 29:35.858
- So sorry.
-  Damn.

29:36.692 --> 29:40.070
Lonnie, who's H?

29:43.657 --> 29:44.909
Helen.

29:46.160 --> 29:47.495
My moms.

29:48.829 --> 29:50.623
You two must be close.

29:51.624 --> 29:53.542
What about the rest of your family?

29:56.253 --> 29:57.671
Just my mom.

29:59.465 --> 30:02.008
After the war...

30:02.009 --> 30:04.303
I wasn't so easy to be around.

30:06.013 --> 30:08.890
Yeah, it's hard going back to normal life.

30:08.891 --> 30:10.975
All three of my brothers served.

30:10.976 --> 30:13.436
Yeah, and both mine served, too.

30:13.437 --> 30:15.523
Jack, the oldest, was a POW.

30:16.565 --> 30:17.942
Yeah?

30:19.485 --> 30:21.194
Where at?

30:21.195 --> 30:22.404
Frankfurt.

30:24.156 --> 30:27.326
Yeah, took him a long time
to get his head right after that.

30:31.747 --> 30:34.375
The Germans got me, too.

30:44.593 --> 30:46.511
Shit.

30:46.512 --> 30:48.222
Sorry. I...

30:51.976 --> 30:54.019
They did something
to you all, didn't they?

31:15.332 --> 31:17.750
Silvermane! Hey, good to see you.

31:17.751 --> 31:19.627
You remember my wife.

31:19.628 --> 31:23.214
Honey, why don't you and Phyllis
go powder your noses?

31:23.215 --> 31:25.133
Eat shit, Alfred.

31:25.134 --> 31:27.386
- Come on, Phyllis.
- It's fine.

31:28.929 --> 31:30.973
Missed you at lunch today, Chief.

31:32.433 --> 31:34.767
Must have been saving room for dinner.

31:34.768 --> 31:36.269
How've you been?

31:36.270 --> 31:38.188
You look good. You in good health?

31:39.273 --> 31:41.608
Strong as ever, my friend.

31:41.609 --> 31:43.651
How about you?

31:43.652 --> 31:46.613
Eh. You know,
the blood pressure's a bit high.

31:46.614 --> 31:48.072
The election, you know.

31:48.073 --> 31:50.950
I do know, seeing as I'm the one
who paid to put you in that seat.

31:50.951 --> 31:54.120
Well, I'm about
to be voted out of it.

31:54.121 --> 31:55.705
And whose fault is that?

31:55.706 --> 31:58.374
You want the whole list
or just the headlines?

31:58.375 --> 32:00.668
Let's just put it down to destiny.

32:00.669 --> 32:02.295
And what?

32:02.296 --> 32:05.215
You just move on to the next guy
and expect me to go quietly?

32:06.675 --> 32:09.093
Only those who will risk going too far

32:09.094 --> 32:12.347
can possibly find out how far one can go.

32:12.348 --> 32:15.683
Well, in that case,
I'd be happy to show you too far.

32:15.684 --> 32:17.895
- I'll just let you fellas talk.
-  Sit down.

32:19.313 --> 32:22.398
Is this about my calling
for an end to Prohibition?

32:22.399 --> 32:25.610
Because I'm simply giving the people
what they want.

32:25.611 --> 32:27.446
Do you think you're special, Morris?

32:28.405 --> 32:32.492
Every four years,
I decide who sits in that chair.

32:32.493 --> 32:34.160
This time, it's going to be Hudson.

32:34.161 --> 32:37.789
Next time, some other asshole.

32:37.790 --> 32:41.876
Well, apparently, this particular asshole
still has some cards left to play.

32:41.877 --> 32:45.296
Why do you think I'm the one
breaking bread with the chief of police?

32:45.297 --> 32:48.091
Fellas, I'm sure
we can reach some kind of--

32:48.092 --> 32:50.510
You've had a good run.

32:50.511 --> 32:52.680
Had to end sometime.

32:54.723 --> 32:56.475
Are you sure about that?

32:57.309 --> 33:00.520
Oh, how silly of me.

33:00.521 --> 33:02.939
I haven't introduced my associate.

33:02.940 --> 33:05.984
Flint, say hello to the mayor.

33:12.950 --> 33:15.034
It's...

33:15.035 --> 33:16.619
it's okay, everybody.

33:16.620 --> 33:18.621
Don't worry. We're all friends here.

33:18.622 --> 33:20.373
It's okay.

33:22.668 --> 33:24.628
I'm not backing down.

33:25.629 --> 33:27.631
Fair enough.

33:29.133 --> 33:31.969
You've got balls, Morris.
I'll give you that much.

33:33.929 --> 33:36.472
May the best man live.

33:41.520 --> 33:43.271
What's next, boss?

33:43.272 --> 33:46.566
He's asked for it. Let's give it to him.

33:52.531 --> 33:55.324
When you were at the station,

33:55.325 --> 33:57.577
where were you going?

33:57.578 --> 33:59.288
Anywhere.

34:00.539 --> 34:01.956
Away.

34:01.957 --> 34:04.585
But if you could choose a place?

34:05.836 --> 34:08.296
Santorini.

34:08.297 --> 34:12.133
It's a Greek island
with black sand beaches

34:12.134 --> 34:15.136
and quaint little towns
with nothing to do

34:15.137 --> 34:19.433
but eat and drink and watch the sunset.

34:20.559 --> 34:23.520
That sounds... really boring.

34:24.646 --> 34:27.440
Well, with the right person...

34:27.441 --> 34:29.443
With the right person?

34:30.360 --> 34:33.738
♪ Last night, I laid a-sleeping ♪

34:33.739 --> 34:37.242
♪ I was thinking to myself ♪

34:38.410 --> 34:39.702
♪ Well...

34:39.703 --> 34:41.454
I'm sorry.

34:41.455 --> 34:43.790
No, don't be.

34:43.791 --> 34:46.210
I didn't picture this.

34:47.294 --> 34:49.587
I did.

34:49.588 --> 34:52.173
We interrupt
your program with a citywide alert.

34:52.174 --> 34:54.592
We have a report coming in.
Authorities ask

34:54.593 --> 34:55.843
that you please stay inside.

34:55.844 --> 34:57.303
- Wait.
- As I speak,

34:57.304 --> 35:00.681
one of these super-powered monsters
is terrorizing the Diamond District.

35:00.682 --> 35:03.059
- Please stay inside...
- It's Flint.

35:03.060 --> 35:05.728
Did you hear me? That has to be Flint.

35:05.729 --> 35:07.688
...as the story develops.
Now, back to your--

35:07.689 --> 35:10.441
Yeah, I heard you. I just don't know
what the hell you want me to do about it.

35:10.442 --> 35:11.984
Well, he was upset
the last time we spoke.

35:11.985 --> 35:13.195
Come on.

35:14.196 --> 35:15.446
I'm trying to help him.

35:15.447 --> 35:17.699
Okay. Then, go.

35:18.700 --> 35:21.744
After everything we've shared--

35:21.745 --> 35:23.621
what he meant to me,
what Ruby meant to you--

35:23.622 --> 35:25.791
are you really going to sit there
and do nothing?

35:29.545 --> 35:31.129
You really are a coward.

35:43.141 --> 35:46.435
All I know is that once it starts,
it gets worse fast.

35:46.436 --> 35:48.437
And there ain't no changing back.

35:48.438 --> 35:50.481
But you should talk to Doc Faber.

35:50.482 --> 35:52.608
She can explain what's going on
a whole lot better than I can.

35:55.487 --> 35:56.363
Robbie.

35:57.239 --> 35:58.991
-  Me? Okay.
- Yeah.

36:02.119 --> 36:04.036
Reilly Investiga--
-  Yeah, it's me.

36:04.037 --> 36:06.122
I don't have time to explain.
Grab your camera,

36:06.123 --> 36:08.792
head down to the Diamond District
right now.

36:29.396 --> 36:31.189
Wait. Wait.

36:32.065 --> 36:34.317
Oh, I...

36:34.318 --> 36:36.694
I-I thought you were someone else.

36:36.695 --> 36:39.156
Well, I know exactly who you are.

36:40.282 --> 36:42.408
The Spider.

36:42.409 --> 36:43.659
The Spider?

36:43.660 --> 36:45.286
Hey, I thought you was dead, huh?

36:45.287 --> 36:46.496
What are you doing he--

36:47.497 --> 36:48.707
Holy shit.

36:49.541 --> 36:50.583
You're here to stop me.

36:50.584 --> 36:52.752
-  No, no. Like I said--
- Hot damn!

36:52.753 --> 36:55.838
Me and The Spider,
duking it out on 6th Ave, huh?

36:55.839 --> 36:57.883
- What?
- Put that on a poster.

36:59.968 --> 37:01.219
Oh. Another one.

37:12.689 --> 37:14.398
Oh! He lives.

37:15.817 --> 37:17.235
Barely.

37:22.282 --> 37:25.077
And now for the main attraction.

37:26.036 --> 37:27.829
♪ Da, da, da ♪

37:38.924 --> 37:41.634
Holy shit. Did you guys see that?

37:41.635 --> 37:43.678
Now who the hell is this guy?

37:43.679 --> 37:45.513
Unbelievable.

37:45.514 --> 37:48.099
Oh, hey, Spider. Want some more?

37:52.396 --> 37:54.647
Come on, man. Fight back.

37:54.648 --> 37:56.649
Do your job. Protect the city.

37:56.650 --> 37:59.860
- Stop Silvermane.
- Save your ass, you mean.

37:59.861 --> 38:01.112
Sir, one of those freaks

38:01.113 --> 38:02.530
is tearing up the Diamond District.

38:02.531 --> 38:04.740
Jesus, Silvermane's not wasting any time.

38:04.741 --> 38:06.575
The Spider is there.

38:06.576 --> 38:08.244
The Spider is there?

38:11.915 --> 38:14.001
Oof. The guy really
should've stayed retired.

38:17.129 --> 38:18.672
Come on. Can we just talk?

38:22.843 --> 38:24.052
I don't know.

38:25.012 --> 38:26.221
Think he's still got it.

38:28.473 --> 38:29.891
Oh. Come on!

38:51.705 --> 38:53.206
Amscray.

39:30.327 --> 39:31.953
Yeah.

39:33.121 --> 39:35.624
Well played, Spider.

39:36.666 --> 39:38.585
But I'm all juiced up.

39:40.087 --> 39:41.462
For now.

39:41.463 --> 39:44.423
The Spider's back! He's back!

39:44.424 --> 39:46.342
Can't you do something?

39:46.343 --> 39:48.887
I'm the goddamn mayor of New York.

39:51.473 --> 39:53.974
-  Happy now?
- Damn it.

39:53.975 --> 39:56.102
Wait. Sir?

39:59.147 --> 40:00.356
Hello.

40:00.357 --> 40:02.692
Come on. Bring it--

40:07.823 --> 40:09.657
That's it. Keep coming.

40:09.658 --> 40:11.408
Oh, you want some more, pal?

40:11.409 --> 40:13.328
I got plenty for you.

40:14.746 --> 40:16.039
Come on.

40:16.540 --> 40:17.499
Missed me.

40:20.043 --> 40:21.293
Ow.

40:21.294 --> 40:22.170
Ah!

40:29.511 --> 40:31.512
You're losing your spark, buddy.

40:31.513 --> 40:33.848
Hey, you had enough, pal?

40:33.849 --> 40:35.183
You're gonna have
to do better than that.

40:41.356 --> 40:43.525
Can I give you
a hand with that?

40:49.739 --> 40:51.574
You see that?

40:51.575 --> 40:53.075
He's still got it.

40:53.076 --> 40:55.328
Yeah. I told you that.

41:00.458 --> 41:02.835
- All right.
- Let's go.

41:02.836 --> 41:04.086
Okay, grab him.

41:05.547 --> 41:07.756
- Okay...
- Wait. Where did you come from?

41:10.010 --> 41:11.343
Back up. Back up.

41:11.344 --> 41:13.430
No, let him through. Let him through.

41:16.474 --> 41:17.558
What's going on here?

41:17.559 --> 41:19.268
Smile for the camera.

41:19.269 --> 41:22.188
Robbie? No. No, no.

41:22.189 --> 41:23.856
We're done here.

41:23.857 --> 41:26.192
- Let go of my hand.
- I have an announcement!

41:26.193 --> 41:29.653
- Me and The Spider have teamed up...
- Not-not a team.

41:29.654 --> 41:31.614
- ...to save this city!
- Not a team. No, not a team.

41:35.118 --> 41:37.328
He's back, everyone.

41:37.329 --> 41:39.455
No. Not back. Not back.

41:39.456 --> 41:41.957
Hey, yeah.

41:41.958 --> 41:43.626
Yeah. One more. One more picture.

41:43.627 --> 41:45.127
- One more, one more.
- I'm good. No, thanks.

41:45.128 --> 41:47.004
Go Spider!

42:20.455 --> 42:22.539
Go away.

42:42.936 --> 42:44.228
Oh.

42:44.229 --> 42:45.688
"Oh" yourself.

42:45.689 --> 42:48.149
Come right on in. Make yourself at home.

43:01.871 --> 43:03.456
Everything cool?

43:07.544 --> 43:09.086
Don't you want to know what happened?

43:09.087 --> 43:11.839
Oh, Flint. Is he okay?

43:11.840 --> 43:13.675
It wasn't him.

43:14.676 --> 43:16.136
What happened to your face?

43:17.178 --> 43:19.805
I... walked into a door.

43:19.806 --> 43:21.599
How many times?

43:28.398 --> 43:30.317
Just tell me one thing.

43:31.318 --> 43:32.443
Am I right?

43:32.444 --> 43:35.821
I think so. W-Well, I don't really know
what you're talking about.

44:04.351 --> 44:07.270
Nice to meet you, Mr. Spider.
